From c64ea14d3f9d55c6df2c4348aa8b89e0cd25c48e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephenuffugus <99242197+Stephenuffugus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:55:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] 3D: restore the prop colormap the models were exported
 without
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every Kenney prop .glb points at a shared palette atlas. Eight of the twelve
(barrel, boulder, chest, crate, crates, pillar, table and the character) EMBED it
in a bufferView; the other four (grass, grass_small, statue, tree) reference it
externally as Textures/colormap.png — and that file was never committed. Three
404s on every load, and those four props rendered untextured.

This is not a substitute palette: the eight embedded copies are byte-identical to
each other (sha256 f9ae1825…, 15794 bytes, 1024x1024 RGBA), so the atlas was
extracted straight out of barrel.glb and written to the path the other four ask
for. Same file the exporter should have shipped.

Verified through the real game: the three requests for
assets/props/Textures/colormap.png now return 200, and the probe's "no 404s on
game assets" check passes with 0 console errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 assets/props/Textures/colormap.png | Bin 0 -> 15794 bytes
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 assets/props/Textures/colormap.png

diff --git a/assets/props/Textures/colormap.png b/assets/props/Textures/colormap.png
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3c36806274363fbe9edb04e8e4d2b46287778418
GIT binary patch
